# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.yarn/install-state.gz

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next
**/.next

# ── Env files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore every env file except the committed example. `.env.*` does not match
# `.env` itself, hence both lines; the negation comes last so it wins
# regardless of what appears above. Without the second line `.env.local` /
# `.env.production` were copied into the build context and `next build`
# inlined any NEXT_PUBLIC_* value they carried into the published image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Project-specific ────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
data
uploads
tests
docs
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
